Short:    Install HTTP/FTP/IRC/SMTP/POP3 server on your BBS
Author:   Giovanni Lambiase, 2:335/253.1@fidonet
Uploader: 3donline@ita.flashnet.it (Renato Cretella)
Type:     comm/TCP

This package is a demo release of WWW-BBS which let you to
install and supply to all your bbs users a fully functional
HTTP/FTP/IRC/SMTP/POP3 server. These are main features:

o  MUI Application
o  Allows you to create a server running following services:
   HTTP,FTP,IRC,SMTP,POP3
o  Fast installation and configuration
o  Allows sysops to give all users a true internet mail box
o  Enable/Disable users
o  Subscription end checks
o  Users can send and receive all mails using standard clients
   (such as YAM, THOR, EUDORA, ...,)
o  Allows you to enable FTP from a CD device

WWW-BBS let you to change in a easy and fast way all settings
of your server, letting you to install and run your server
in 5 minutes.

The main aim of WWW-BBS is to let all sysops to make a true
internet mail box for all users. WWW-BBS can also manage
end subscription date if you want users pay for it.

NOTE: This is a demo release. FTP, IRC and MAIL management is
      not present. Furthermore, using a modem, you can connect
      to the server up to 5 minutes.
